docs/library-packages-upgrade/justifications/T-20.md:232:- **`post.body` no longer available in Content Layer API**: The `estimateReadTime` function in `getThreadDetail.ts` previously used `post.body` (the raw markdown string) to estimate reading time. In the Content Layer API, `body` is not stored on the entry object. The function now defaults to 1 minute for all articles (the fallback when body is `undefined`). This means thread read time estimates will show "1 min" per article rather than actual word-count-based estimates. This is a functional regression but visually acceptable for the current scope. A proper fix would require a custom loader or storing word counts in frontmatter — deferred to a content task outside this campaign's scope (design §7 out-of-scope: content rewrites).
